t (4), which is 400. Multiply 978 by 400:\n\nFirst compute 978×4 = ?\n\n900×4=3600,\n\n70×4=280,\n\n8×4=32,\n\nTotal: 3600+280=3880; 3880+32=3912. Then multiply by 100 (since it\'s the hundreds place), so 3912×100=391,200. Third partial product is 391,200.\n\nNow, add all three partial products together:\n\n4890 (from ones) + 29,340 (tens) + 391,200 (hundreds).\n\nFirst add 4890 + 29,340:\n\n4890 + 29,340 = 34,230 (since 4,890 + 29,340: 4k +29k=33k; 890+340=1,230 → total 34,230)\n\nThen add 34,230 + 391,200:\n\n34,230 + 391,200 = 425,430 (since 34k + 391k = 425k; 230 + 200 = 430 → total 425,430)\n\nTherefore, the final product should be 425,430.\n\nWait, let me verify with another method to ensure accuracy. Let\'s use the standard multiplication steps:\n\n       978  \n     × 435  \n     --------\n       4890   (978 × 5)\n      29340   (978 × 30, shifted one position)\n     391200   (978 × 400, shifted two positions)\n     --------\n     425430\n\nYes, adding those gives 425,430. So that\'s correct. I think my initial confusion was because I started with a different problem in my head, but now focusing on 978×435, the result is 425,430.\n\nWait, let me do a quick check using another method, maybe the distributive property:\n\n978 × 435 = 978 × (400 + 30 +5) = 978×400 + 978×30 + 978×5, which is exactly what I did. So that\'s correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using a calculator check? Well, since I can\'t use a calculator, but let\'s see:\n\nCompute 1000 × 435 = 435,000. Since 978 is 22 less than 1000, so subtract 22×435 from 435,000.\n\n22×400 = 8,800; 22×35=770 → total 8,800 +770 =9,570. So 435,000 - 9,570 = 425,430. Yep, same result. So that confirms it.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 425,430.\n\nBut in the initial thought process, I had some muddled numbers where I was mixing up different problems. But upon correcting myself and focusing on the given numbers, it\'s clear. So the steps are:\n\n1. Multiply 978 by 5 (ones place) = 4,890\n\n2. Multiply 978 by 30 (tens place) = 29,340\n\n3. Multiply 978 by 400 (hundreds place) = 391,200\n\nSum all three: 4,890 +29,340 =34,230; 34,230 +391,200=425,430\n\nSo the final answer is 425,430.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 978 and 435 is \\boxed{425430}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 978 and 435, we break it down into three steps based on the place values of the digits in 435 (ones, tens, and hundreds).\n\n1. **Multiply 978 by the ones place digit (5):**\n   \\[\n   978 \\times 5 = 4890\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 978 by the tens place digit (30):**\n   \\[\n   978 \\times 30 = 29340\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 978 by the hundreds place digit (400):**\n   \\[\n   978 \\times 400 = 391200\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three multiplications:\n\\[\n4890 + 29340 + 391200\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the ones and tens place multiplications:\n\\[\n4890 + 29340 = 34230\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to the hundreds place multiplication:\n\\[\n34230 + 391200 = 425430\n\\]\n\nThus, the final product of 978 and 435 is \\(\\boxed{425430}\\).', '']  0%|          | 2/500 [03:56<17:55:47, 129.61s/it]
