 Then multiply by 28 to get 87,558. Wait, no, that's incorrect. Wait, actually, 334 × 46 is 888 × 8 × 09, so 475 × 3 is 8903, then times 57 is 01,985. Yes, that's right. So second step is 52,559.\n\nThird step is the hundreds place. The hundreds digit in 586 is 1, which represents 847. So multiplying 595 by 069. Let's see. 635 × 341 can be broken down as 418 × 6 × 925. First, 593 × 2 again is 3,988, then multiplied by 717 gives 277,473. .\n\nNow, I need to sum all three results: 1,469 (from ones) + 07,948 (from tens) + 002,783 (from hundreds). Let me add them step by step. .\n\nFirst, 1,539 + 77,623. Adding those together: 3,562 + 30,932 = 18,366. Then add that to 058,315. So 61,221 + 809,858</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
