2 = 760,000 - 1,520 = 758,480. That matches. So the answer is 758,480.\n\nTherefore, following the template steps:\n\n1. Multiply 760 by 8 (ones digit): 6,080\n\n2. Multiply 760 by 90 (tens digit is 9, so 9×10): 68,400\n\n3. Multiply 760 by 900 (hundreds digit is 9, so 9×100): 684,000\n\nSumming them: 6,080 + 68,400 = 74,480; then 74,480 + 684,000 = 758,480.\n\nSo the reasoning should be structured like that.\n\nI think in my initial wrong attempt I confused the numbers, but now corrected. Need to present this step-by-step as per the example.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe final computed product is \\boxed{758480}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 760 and 998?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 998 has three digits, so we can break it down into hundreds, tens, and ones places:\n1. Multiply 760 by the ones place digit 8 of 998:\n   \\[\n   760 \\times 8 = 6,\\!080\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 760 by the tens place digit 90 of 998 (since the tens digit is 9, it represents \\(9 \\times 10\\)):\n   \\[\n   760 \\times 90 = 760 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 6,\\!840 \\times 10 = 68,\\!400\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 760 by the hundreds place digit 900 of 998 (since the hundreds digit is 9, it represents \\(9 \\times 100\\)):\n   \\[\n   760 \\times 900 = 760 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 6,\\!840 \\times 100 = 684,\\!000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n6,\\!080 + 68,\\!400 + 684,\\!000 = 758,\\!480\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{758480}.", '']
