. **Multiply 731 by the tens place digit (60):**\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 60 = 731 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 4386 \\times 10 = 43860\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 731 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 900 = 731 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 6579 \\times 100 = 657900\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results from each step:\n\\[\n1462 + 43860 + 657900\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the first two steps:\n\\[\n1462 + 43860 = 45322\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to the third step:\n\\[\n45322 + 657900 = 703222\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 731 and 962 is \\(\\boxed{703222}\\).", '']
