 1*100): 790*100 = 79,000.\n\nNow add all three results: 6,320 + 71,100 = 77,420. Then 77,420 + 79,000 = 156,420. So same result. That's good.\n\nTherefore, the product is 156,420. I think that's correct. Let me verify with another method. Maybe using the distributive property again: 198 is 200 - 2, so as before, 790*200 = 158,000 minus 790*2=1,580 gives 156,420. Yep, same answer. Okay, so I'm confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
