.\n\nBut let me check if there was a miscalculation in the multiplication steps.\n\nWait, 821 \u00d7 6 is indeed 4926, so \u00d7100 is 492,600. That's correct.\n\n821 \u00d710 is 8210. Correct.\n\n821 \u00d78 is 6,568. Correct.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n6,568 + 8,210:\n\n6,568 +8,000 =14,568, plus 210 \u219214,568+210=14,778. Then adding 492,600 gives 507,378.\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 507,378.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 821 and 618 is \\boxed{507378}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 821 and 618, we can break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of the digits in 618.\n\n1. **Multiply 821 by the ones place digit (8):**\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 8 = 6568\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   \\[\n   800 \\times 8 = 6400, \\quad 20 \\times 8 = 160, \\quad 1 \\times 8 = 8\n   \\]\n   Summing these results:\n   \\[\n   6400 + 160 + 8 = 6568\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 821 by the tens place digit (10):**\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 10 = 8210\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 821 by the hundreds place digit (600):**\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 600 = 492600\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 6 = 4926 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 100)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4926 \\times 100 = 492600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results from the steps:**\n   \\[\n   6568 + 8210 + 492600\n   \\]\n   First, add the first two results:\n   \\[\n   6568 + 8210 = 14778\n   \\]\n   Then add the third result:\n   \\[\n   14778 + 492600 = 507378\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final product of 821 and 618 is \\(\\boxed{507378}\\).",
