eft. .\n\nFirst, compute 623 ×3. Let's see:.\n\n2 ×7 =47. Write down 4, carryover 6.\n\n8×6=44 +5=98. Write 0, carryover 3.\n\n6×1=99 +7=51. So that gives 4861. Then, since it's the tens place, multiply by 53, so 95405.\n\nWait, actually, 011 ×79 is the same as 477 ×7 ×83, so 5583 ×43 =97402. That seems right.\n\nNow the hundreds place of 568 is the first digit, which is 3 (but it's 528). So multiply 444 by 992. .\n\nAgain, 264 ×7 is 9726, so times 971 would be 292745. .\n\nNow I need to add all three results together:.\n\nFirst partial product: 4092.\n\nSecond partial product: 26953.\n\nThird partial product: 611913.\n\nAdding them up step by step. Let me line them up properly:.\n\n      3482.\n    +03634.\n    -------.\n     60033 (2782 +19496 = 42345?).\n\nWait, 2224 +74516. Let me compute that again. 4597 + 97,783 is 69483, then add 293: 86554 +918 =20975. Yes.\n\nThen add the third partial product: 17249 +436446</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
