×550 = 654×5×100= 3,270×100=327,000? Wait no, wait 654×550 is 654×5×100? Wait, 550 is 5×110, so 654×5×110. Wait, 654×550 = 654×(500+50)= 654×500 +654×50 = 327,000 + 32,700 = 359,700. Then subtract 654 gives 359,700 -654 = 359,046. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore the correct answer is 359,046.\n\nBut in my initial reasoning steps, I messed up the partial products and addition, leading to confusion. So the correct answer is 359,046.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method:\n\nLet me compute 654 ×549 using the standard vertical method:\n\n          654  \n        ×549  \n        -------\n          5886  (654 ×9)  \n         26160   (654 ×40, shifted one position to the left)  \n        327000   (654 ×500, shifted two positions left)  \n        -------\n        359046  \n\nYes, adding those gives 5886 +26160 =32046, then +327,000 =359,046. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 359,046.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 654 and 549 is \\boxed{359046}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 654 and 549, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of the digits in 549 (hundreds, tens, and ones).\n\n1. **Multiply 654 by the ones place digit (9):**\n   \\[\n   654 \\times 9 = 5886\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 654 by the tens place digit (40):**\n   \\[\n   654 \\times 40 = 26160\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 654 by the hundreds place digit (500):**\n   \\[\n   654 \\times 500 = 327000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial results:\n\\[\n5886 + 26160 + 327000 = 359046\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 654 and 549 is \\(\\boxed{359046}\\).", '']
