      "text": "123,456. Wait, but I think I messed up the partial products. Let me try again step by step.\n\nWait, maybe I need to recast the problem properly. Let me start over with the given numbers: 311 and 277. The question is to compute 311 \u00d7 277.\n\nSo, first, break down 277 into 200 + 70 +7.\n\nTherefore, the product is 311*(200 +70 +7) = 311\u00d7200 +311\u00d770 +311\u00d77.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n311 \u00d7 200 = 311 \u00d7 2 \u00d7 100 = 622 \u00d7 100 = 62,200.\n\n311 \u00d770 = 311 \u00d77 \u00d710 = (300\u00d77 +11\u00d77) \u00d710 = (2,100 +77) \u00d710 = 2,177 \u00d710 =21,770.\n\n311 \u00d77 = (300\u00d77) + (11\u00d77) =2,100 +77 =2,177.\n\nAdding all three together: 62,200 +21,770 =83,970; then 83,970 +2,177 =86,147.\n\nSo the total should be 86,147.\n\nWait, let me check the arithmetic again:\n\n62,200 +21,770:\n\n62,200 +20,000 =82,200; then +1,770 =83,970. Correct.\n\nThen 83,970 +2,177:\n\n83,970 +2,000 =85,970; then +177 =86,147. Yes, that's right.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\u2003\u2003311\n\n\u00d7277\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply by 7 (ones place):\n\n311 \u00d77 =2,177.\n\nThen multiply by 7 (tens place, so shifted one position left):\n\n311 \u00d77 =2,177, but shifted one left is 21,770.\n\nThen multiply by 2 (hundreds place, shifted two left):\n\n311 \u00d72 =622, shifted two left is 62,200.\n\nNow adding those three:\n\n2,177\n\n+21,770\n\n=23,947? Wait, no: 2,177 +21,770 =23,947? Let me add:\n\n2,177 +21,770:\n\n2,000 +21,000 =23,000; 177 +770 =947. So total 23,947. Then add 62,200:\n\n23,947 +62,200 =86,147. Correct.\n\nTherefore the final answer is 86,147. I think my first attempt had some confusion with the numbers, but redoing it carefully gives this result. So the steps are correct when broken down properly.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 311 and 277 is \\boxed{86147}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 311 and 277, we can break down the multiplication into steps by considering each digit of 277 (200, 70, and 7) and then summing the results.\n\n1. Multiply 311 by the ones place digit (7):\n   \\[\n   311 \\times 7 = 2177\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 311 by the tens place digit (70). Note that this result needs to be shifted one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   311 \\times 70 = 311 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 2177 \\times 10 = 21770\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 311 by the hundreds place digit (200). Note that this result needs to be shifted two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   311 \\times 200 = 311 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 622 \\times 100 = 62200\n   \\]\n\nSumming all the results from the steps above:\n\\[\n2177 + 21770 + 62200 = 86147\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 311 and 277 is \\(\\boxed{86147}\\).",
