e results.\n\n1. Multiply 311 by the ones place digit (7):\n   \\[\n   311 \\times 7 = 2177\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 311 by the tens place digit (70). Note that this result needs to be shifted one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   311 \\times 70 = 311 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 2177 \\times 10 = 21770\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 311 by the hundreds place digit (200). Note that this result needs to be shifted two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   311 \\times 200 = 311 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 622 \\times 100 = 62200\n   \\]\n\nSumming all the results from the steps above:\n\\[\n2177 + 21770 + 62200 = 86147\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 311 and 277 is \\(\\boxed{86147}\\).", '']
