 digit of 693 is 9. Since it's the tens place, it's 90. So multiply 463 × 90. That's the same as 463×9×10.\n\nFirst compute 463 ×9:\n\n9×3=27 (ones place, write 7 carryover 2)\n9×6=54 +2=56 (tens place, write 6 carryover 5)\n9×4=36 +5=41 (hundreds place, write 1 carryover 4)\nThousands place: carryover 4. So 4167. Then multiply by 10: 41,670.\n\nNow the hundreds place digit of 693 is 6, which is actually 600. Multiply 463 ×600.\n\nFirst compute 463×6:\n\n6×3=18 (ones place, write 8 carryover 1)\n6×6=36 +1=37 (tens place, write 7 carryover 3)\n6×4=24 +3=27 (hundreds place, write 7 carryover 2)\nThousands place: carryover 2. So 2778. Then multiply by 100: 277,800.\n\nNow add all three partial products:\n\nFirst partial product: 1,389\n\nSecond partial product: 41,670\n\nThird partial product: 277,800\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\n1,389 + 41,670 = 43,059\n\nThen add 277,800: 43,059 + 277,800 = 320,859.\n\nWait, let me verify:\n\n1389 + 41670 = 43,059 (correct)\n\n43,059 + 277,800:\n\n43,059 + 200,000 = 243,059\n\n243,059 + 77,800 = 320,859. Yes.\n\nAlternatively, using another method:\n\n463 × 693 = ?\n\nLet me use distributive property:\n\n463 × (700 - 7) = 463×700 - 463×7\n\n463×700 = 324,100 (since 463×7=3,241; times 100 is 324,100)\n\n463×7 = 3,241\n\nThus, 324,100 - 3,241 = 320,859. Same result.\n\nSo the final answer should be 320,859.\n\nBut let me check again step by step:\n\nFirst partial product (3×463=1,389)\n\nSecond (90×463=41,670)\n\nThird (600×463=277,800)\n\nTotal: 1,389 +41,670 = 43,059; 43,059 +277,800 = 320,859. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 320,859.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 463 and 693 is \\boxed{320859}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 463 and 693, we can break down the multiplication step by step using the standard multiplication method.\n\n1. **Multiply 463 by the ones place digit (3) of 693:**\n   \\[\n   463 \\times 3 = 1389\n   \\]\n   Result: 1389\n\n2. **Multiply 463 by the tens place digit (90) of 693:**\n   \\[\n   463 \\times 90 = 463 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 4167 \\times 10 = 41670\n   \\]\n   Result: 41670\n\n3. **Multiply 463 by the hundreds place digit (600) of 693:**\n   \\[\n   463 \\times 600 = 463 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 2778 \\times 100 = 277800\n   \\]\n   Result: 277800\n\n4. **Sum all the partial results:**\n   \\[\n   1389 + 41670 + 277800 = 320859\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 463 and 693 is \\(\\boxed{320859}\\).", ''] 13%|#3        | 65/500 [1:34:40<11:01:26, 91.23s/it]
