alculator steps:\n\n532 \u00d7 600 = 532 *6 *100 = 3192*100 = 319200\n\n532 \u00d710 =5320\n\n532 \u00d79 =4788\n\nAdding all together: 319200 +5320 = 324,520; then +4,788 = 329,308. Yes.\n\nSo the answer is 329,308.\n\nBut let me check again with another approach, perhaps cross-multiplying:\n\n532 \u00d7619\n\nBreakdown:\n\n(500 +32) \u00d7 (600 +19)\n\n=500\u00d7600 +500\u00d719 +32\u00d7600 +32\u00d719\n\n=300,000 + 9,500 +19,200 +608\n\n300,000 +9,500 is 309,500\n\n309,500 +19,200 = 328,700\n\n328,700 +608 = 329,308. Same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the reasoning should follow the step-by-step multiplication by each digit and summing the partial products.\n</think>\n\n",
