Yes, that's correct. So the final answer should be 345,114.\n\nWait, so in my initial reasoning when I first thought through, I must have mixed up numbers. Probably confused 693 with another number. So the correct answer is 345,114. Let me confirm with another method, like the distributive property:\n\n(500 - 2) \u00d7 (700 - 7) ?\n\nWait 693 is 700 -7, and 498 is 500-2. Let's see:\n\n(500 - 2)(700 - 7) = 500\u00d7700 -500\u00d77 -2\u00d7700 +2\u00d77\n\n= 350,000 - 3,500 - 1,400 + 14\n\n= 350,000 - 4,900 +14 = 345,114. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 345,114. I must have made a mistake in my first calculation when I was thinking through the partial products, probably because I was getting distracted. So the correct answer is 345,114.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 498 and 693 is \\boxed{345114}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 498 and 693, we can break down the multiplication step by step using the standard algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 498 by the ones place digit (3) of 693:**\n   \\[\n   498 \\times 3 = 1494\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 498 by the tens place digit (90) of 693:**\n   \\[\n   498 \\times 90 = 498 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 4482 \\times 10 = 44820\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 498 by the hundreds place digit (600) of 693:**\n   \\[\n   498 \\times 600 = 498 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 2988 \\times 100 = 298800\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n1494 + 44820 + 298800\n\\]\n\nAdding these step by step:\n\\[\n1494 + 44820 = 46314\n\\]\n\\[\n46314 + 298800 = 345114\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 498 and 693 is \\(\\boxed{345114}\\).",
