ct answer is 684,019.\n\nI must have made a mistake in my initial thinking by possibly miscalculating the digits or steps. But following this method carefully gives 684,019. Let me verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n       703\n     \u00d7973\n     -------\n       2109   (703 \u00d73)\n     49210    (703 \u00d770, shifted one position)\n   632700     (703 \u00d7900, shifted two positions)\n   -----------\n     684019\n\nYes, adding those three lines:\n\n2109\n\n+49210 \u2192 51319\n\n+632700 \u2192 684,019. Correct.\n\nSo the correct answer is 684,019. I must have confused the numbers in my first attempt, but now it's clear.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 703 and 973 is \\boxed{684019}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 703 and 973, we break down the multiplication into three steps based on the digits of 973 (which are 9, 7, and 3 in the hundreds, tens, and ones places respectively):\n\n1. **Multiply 703 by the ones place digit (3):**\n   \\[\n   703 \\times 3 = 2109\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 703 by the tens place digit (70):**\n   \\[\n   703 \\times 70 = 703 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 4921 \\times 10 = 49210\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 703 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   703 \\times 900 = 703 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 6327 \\times 100 = 632700\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three multiplications:\n\\[\n2109 + 49210 = 51319\n\\]\n\\[\n51319 + 632700 = 684019\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 703 and 973 is \\(\\boxed{684019}\\).",
