 total is 631,150. But in my initial calculation when I thought of 971 as 900+70+1, I also got 631,150. So why did I get confused earlier?\n\nAh, in the first version where I thought of 650 as 600+50+0, so multiplying each part by 971:\n\n971 *600 = 582,600\n\n971*50=48,550\n\n971*0=0\n\nAdding those gives 582,600 +48,550 = 631,150. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 631,150. The confusion earlier was because of a miscalculation in the standard algorithm when I first thought of 971*6 as 5,850 instead of 5,826. So the error was mine in that step.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 631,150.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 971 and 650 is \\boxed{631150}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 971 and 650, we can break down the multiplication into smaller steps using the distributive property.\n\n1. **Multiply 971 by 600**:\n   \\[\n   971 \\times 600 = 971 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 5826 \\times 100 = 582600\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 971 by 50**:\n   \\[\n   971 \\times 50 = 971 \\times 5 \\times 10 = 4855 \\times 10 = 48550\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 971 by 0 (the ones place of 650)**:\n   \\[\n   971 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n582600 + 48550 + 0 = 631150\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 971 and 650 is \\(\\boxed{631150}\\).", '']
