ace digit (50) of 754:**\n   \\[\n   802 \\times 50 = 40100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 802 by the hundreds place digit (700) of 754:**\n   \\[\n   802 \\times 700 = 561400\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\n\\[\n3208 + 40100 + 561400 = 604708\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{604708}\\).\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 802 and 754 is \\boxed{604708}.",
