ether:\n\nFirst: 447\n\nSecond: 10,430\n\nThird:14,900\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\nFirst add 447 +10,430 = 10,877\n\nThen add 14,900 to that: 10,877 +14,900.\n\nLet's compute that: 10,000 +14,000 =24,000; 877 +900 =1,777. So total is 24,000 +1,777 =25,777? Wait, no, wait. Wait 10,877 +14,900:\n\nBreak down:\n\n10,877 +10,000 =20,877\n\n20,877 +4,900 =25,777.\n\nSo total is 25,777.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, compute 149 \u00d7173:\n\nLet me do 149 \u00d7173:\n\nFirst, 149 \u00d7100 =14,900\n\n149 \u00d770 =10,430\n\n149 \u00d73 =447\n\nAdding those together: 14,900 +10,430 =25,330; 25,330 +447 =25,777. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, using another multiplication method:\n\n149 \u00d7173\n\nMultiply 149 \u00d7 170 first, then add 149 \u00d73.\n\n149 \u00d7170 =149 \u00d717 \u00d710.\n\n149 \u00d717:\n\nCompute 149\u00d710=1,490\n\n149\u00d77=1,043\n\nAdding those gives 1,490 +1,043 =2,533. Then \u00d710 is 25,330.\n\nThen add 149\u00d73=447, total 25,330+447=25,777. Same result.\n\nTherefore, the product is 25,777.\n\nWait but in my initial wrong thinking I was mixing up numbers, but now corrected, the correct answer is 25,777.\n\nWait let me confirm once more with calculator steps:\n\n149 \u00d7173:\n\nCompute 149 \u00d7 173:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n173 \u00d7100 =17,300\n\n173 \u00d740 =6,920\n\n173 \u00d79 =1,557\n\nAdd them together: 17,300 +6,920 =24,220; 24,220 +1,557 =25,777. Yep, same result.\n\nSo the final answer should be 25,777. I need to present that in the template given.\n\nWait the template requires:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 149 and 173?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 173 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 149 by the ones place digit 3 of 173: 149 \u00d73 = 447\n2. Multiply 149 by the tens place digit 70 of 173: 149 \u00d770 = 10,430\n3. Multiply 149 by the hundreds place digit 100 of 173: 149 \u00d7100 =14,900\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step re