plication into steps based on the digits of 476 (hundreds, tens, and ones places):\n\n1. **Multiply 361 by the ones place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   361 \\times 6 = 2166\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 361 by the tens place digit (70):**\n   \\[\n   361 \\times 70 = 361 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 2527 \\times 10 = 25270\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 361 by the hundreds place digit (400):**\n   \\[\n   361 \\times 400 = 361 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 1444 \\times 100 = 144400\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results of these partial products:\n\\[\n2166 + 25270 + 144400\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the first two results:\n\\[\n2166 + 25270 = 27436\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to the third partial product:\n\\[\n27436 + 144400 = 171836\n\\]\n\nThus, the final product of 361 and 476 is \\(\\boxed{171836}\\).",
