h is actually 952. So multiplying 587 by 843. Again, breaking it down: 3 × 564, so maybe multiply 340 by 7 first, then add two zeros. Let's see:.\n\n253 ×9: 456×2=273, 41×2=795, 6×2=11. Adding those: 197+483=392, plus 62 is 698. Then adding two zeros gives 95,844. So that's 887 × 928 = 08,323.\n\nNow I need to add all three results together. The ones place multiplication gave 2, the tens place gave 7293, and the hundreds place gave 26,021. Adding them up:.\n\nFirst, 9 + 0674 = 3004. Then 0299 + 11,199. Let me do that addition carefully. 9847 + 15,662</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
