find the product of 624 and 159, we break down the multiplication using the place values of 159 (100, 50, and 9):\n\n1. **Multiply 624 by the ones place digit (9):**\n   \\[\n   624 \\times 9 = 5616\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 624 by the tens place digit (50):**\n   \\[\n   624 \\times 50 = 624 \\times 5 \\times 10 = 3120 \\times 10 = 31200\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 624 by the hundreds place digit (100):**\n   \\[\n   624 \\times 100 = 62400\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n5616 + 31200 + 62400\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(5616\\) and \\(31200\\):\n\\[\n5616 + 31200 = 36816\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to \\(62400\\):\n\\[\n36816 + 62400 = 99216\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{99216}\\).", '']
