) =453×300 +453×36.\n\nWait, but maybe do it as (450+3)(336):\n\n450×336 +3×336.\n\n450×336: 450×300=135,000; 450×36=16,200 → total 135,000+16,200=151,200.\n\n3×336=1,008.\n\nTotal 151,200 +1,008=152,208. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, use standard multiplication:\n\n      453\n\n    ×336\n\n    --------\n\n      2718   (453×6)\n\n    13590    (453×30, shifted one position)\n\n   135900    (453×300, shifted two positions)\n\n    ---------\n\n    152,208\n\nYes, that matches. So the correct answer is 152,208.\n\nWait, but in my initial calculation when I was thinking, I messed up with different numbers (like 189×819), but the actual problem here is 453×336. So the final answer is 152,208.\n\nTherefore, the reasoning should follow the steps as:\n\n1. Multiply 453 by 6 (ones place): 2718\n\n2. Multiply 453 by 30 (tens place): 13,590\n\n3. Multiply 453 by 300 (hundreds place): 135,900\n\nSum them all: 2718 +13,590 =16,308; then +135,900 =152,208.\n\nSo the answer is 152,208.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 453 and 336 is \\boxed{152208}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 453 and 336, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of 336 (300, 30, and 6):\n\n1. **Multiply 453 by 6 (ones place):**\n   \\[\n   453 \\times 6 = 2718\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(400 \\times 6 = 2400\\), \\(50 \\times 6 = 300\\), \\(3 \\times 6 = 18\\). Summing these gives \\(2400 + 300 + 18 = 2718\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 453 by 30 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   453 \\times 30 = 13590\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(453 \\times 3 = 1359\\), then multiply by 10 to get \\(13590\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 453 by 300 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   453 \\times 300 = 135900\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(453 \\times 3 = 1359\\), then multiply by 100 to get \\(135900\\).\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\n- First, add the results of the ones and tens place multiplications:\n  \\[\n  2718 + 13590 = 16308\n  \\]\n\n- Then, add the result of the hundreds place multiplication:\n  \\[\n  16308 + 135900 = 152208\n  \\]\n\nThus, the final product of 453 and 336 is \\(\\boxed{152208}\\).", ''] 27%|##6       | 134/500 [2:53:16<10:27:02, 102.79s/it]
