\n\nCompute 120*900 = 108,000\n\n120*27 = 3,240\n\nSo total is 108,000 + 3,240 = 111,240. So that matches the second method. Therefore, my first approach was wrong because I broke it down into 900+20+7, but when multiplying by 120, the 20 is 20*1 (the tens place), so 20*120 = 2,400. Then adding 120*900 (108,000) + 120*20 (2,400) + 120*7 (840). Wait, that would be 108,000 + 2,400 is 110,400 plus 840 is 111,240. So that's correct. So in my first approach, I must have miscalculated when I said 120*200 (which would be if it were the hundreds place, but 927's tens digit is 2, so it's 20, not 200). So my mistake was in the first step when I thought the tens place was 200. So the correct answer is 111,240.\n\nAlright, so I need to correct my reasoning. Let me structure it properly now.\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 120 and 927?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 927 has three digits, so we can break it down into hundreds, tens, and ones places.\n\n1. Multiply 120 by the ones place digit (7):\n   120 \u00d7 7 = 840\n\n2. Multiply 120 by the tens place digit (20):\n   120 \u00d7 20 = 2,400\n\n3. Multiply 120 by the hundreds place digit (900):\n   120 \u00d7 900 = 108,000\n\nNow, sum all the step results: 840 + 2,400 + 108,000.\n\nFirst, 840 + 2,400 = 3,240.\n\nThen, 3,240 + 108,000 = 111,240.\n\nAnswer:\nSo, the final computed product is 111,240.",
