indeed 88,400. And 442 \u00d73 is 1,326. So total is correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 89,726. \n\nBut wait, let me do the multiplication another way to confirm. 442 \u00d7 203 can be written as 442 \u00d7 (200 + 3) = 442\u00d7200 + 442\u00d73 = same as before. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard algorithm:\n\n     442\n   \u00d7 203\n   -------\n     1326  (442 \u00d7 3)\n   0000   (442 \u00d7 0, shifted one position)\n  88400   (442 \u00d7 2, shifted two positions)\n   -------\n   89726\n\nYes, adding those gives 1,326 + 88,400 = 89,726. So the correct answer is 89,726.\n\nI think my initial confusion was because I started with a different example in my head, but now focusing on the given numbers, it's clear. The key steps are breaking down 203 into its place values, multiplying each by 442, and adding the results. The middle step (tens place) is zero, so it doesn't contribute. The hundreds place is 200, so that's 88,400. Adding the ones place gives the total. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be 89,726.\n\n\n\n",
