e correct answer is 501,030. I need to make sure to follow the steps properly this time.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 879 and 570?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 570 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 879 by the ones place digit 0 of 570: \\(879 \\times 0 = 0\\).\n2. Multiply 879 by the tens place digit 70 of 570: \\(879 \\times 70 = 61,\\!530\\).\n3. Multiply 879 by the hundreds place digit 500 of 570: \\(879 \\times 500 = 439,\\!500\\).\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(0 + 61,\\!530 + 439,\\!500 = 501,\\!030\\).\nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{501030}\\).",
