 1,911 = 7,371. Then multiply by 10 gives 73,710. Yep, same result.\n\nSo the correct answer should be 73,710. I think I made a mistake in my initial reasoning because I was confused with different numbers. Let me make sure the steps are clear in the template.\n\nSo applying the template:\n\nThe question is 273 and 270.\n\nReasoning steps:\n\n1. Multiply 273 by the ones digit of 270 (0): 273 \u00d7 0 = 0.\n\n2. Multiply 273 by the tens digit (70): 273 \u00d7 70 = 273 \u00d7 7 \u00d7 10 = 1,911 \u00d7 10 = 19,110.\n\n3. Multiply 273 by the hundreds digit (200): 273 \u00d7 200 = 54,600.\n\nThen sum them: 0 + 19,110 + 54,600 = 73,710.\n\nSo the final answer is 73,710. That seems right.\n\nI think I initially messed up because I was looking at the example with different numbers and got confused, but now I've clarified it. Let me ensure each step is properly written in the template.\n\n</think>\n\n",
