values of the digits in 960 (hundreds, tens, and ones).\n\n1. **Multiply 666 by the ones place digit (0):**\n   \\[\n   666 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 666 by the tens place digit (60):**\n   \\[\n   666 \\times 60 = 666 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 3996 \\times 10 = 39960\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 666 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   666 \\times 900 = 666 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 5994 \\times 100 = 599400\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n0 + 39960 + 599400 = 639360\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 666 and 960 is \\(\\boxed{639360}\\).",
