\n\nWait, but let me verify using another method to be sure. Let's do standard multiplication:\n\n   720\n\u00d7 348\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 720 by 8: 5,760.\n\nThen multiply 720 by 40 (shift one position to the left): 28,800.\n\nThen multiply 720 by 300 (shift two positions left): 216,000.\n\nAdding them all gives 5,760 + 28,800 = 34,560; 34,560 + 216,000 = 250,560. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, compute 720 \u00d7 348:\n\nLet me compute 720 \u00d7 300 = 216,000\n\n720 \u00d7 40 = 28,800\n\n720 \u00d7 8 = 5,760\n\nAdding all gives same as above. So the answer should be 250,560.\n\nTherefore, the template answer would follow the steps as outlined.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 720 and 348?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 348 has three digits, so we break it down:  \n1. Multiply 720 by the **ones place digit** (8):  \n   \\(720 \\times 8 = 5,\\!760\\).  \n2. Multiply 720 by the **tens place digit** (40):  \n   \\(720 \\times 40 = 28,\\!800\\).  \n3. Multiply 720 by the **hundreds place digit** (300):  \n   \\(720 \\times 300 = 216,\\!000\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(5,\\!760 + 28,\\!800 + 216,\\!000 = 250,\\!560\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{250560}\\).",
