8    (628 \u00d7 60, shifted one position)\n 314000    (628 \u00d7 500, shifted two positions)\n   -------\n  352308\n\nYes, adding those gives 352,308. So that's the correct answer.\n\nI think earlier I confused the numbers because I started with a different example, but now correcting that, the answer should be 352,308.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 628 and 561 is \\boxed{352308}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 628 and 561, we can break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of 561 (which is 500 + 60 + 1):\n\n1. Multiply 628 by the ones place digit (1):\n   \\[\n   628 \\times 1 = 628\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 628 by the tens place digit (60):\n   \\[\n   628 \\times 60 = 628 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 3768 \\times 10 = 37680\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 628 by the hundreds place digit (500):\n   \\[\n   628 \\times 500 = 628 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 3140 \\times 100 = 314000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n628 + 37680 + 314000\n\\]\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n\\[\n628 + 37680 = 38308\n\\]\n\\[\n38308 + 314000 = 352308\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{352308}\\).",
