ucts:\n\nFirst: \xa0\xa06,111\n\nSecond: 69,840\n\nThird:261,900\n\nAdding first two: 6,111 + 69,840 = 75,951\n\nThen add 261,900 + 75,951 = 337,851.\n\nWait, let me check that addition again:\n\n6,111\n\n+69,840\n\n= 6,111 + 60,000 = 66,111; then +9,840 = 75,951. Yes.\n\nThen 75,951 + 261,900:\n\n75,951 + 200,000 = 275,951\n\n275,951 + 61,900 = 337,851\n\nYes. So the total product is 337,851.\n\nWait, but let me confirm using another method to ensure accuracy.\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property:\n\n873 × 387 = 873 × (400 - 13) = 873×400 - 873×13.\n\nCompute 873×400 = 873×4×100 = 3,492 × 100 = 349,200.\n\nThen compute 873×13:\n\n873×10 = 8,730\n\n873×3 = 2,619\n\nAdding those: 8,730 + 2,619 = 11,349.\n\nSubtract: 349,200 - 11,349 = 337,851. Same result. Good.\n\nAlternatively, using standard multiplication again step by step:\n\nLet me recheck the partial products:\n\nFirst step (7):\n\n873 ×7:\n\n7×3=21 → 1, carry 2.\n\n7×7=49 +2=51 →1, carry 5.\n\n7×8=56 +5=61 →1, carry6. So 6111. Correct.\n\nSecond step (80):\n\n873×8=6984 → shifted by one → 69,840. Correct.\n\nThird step (300):\n\n873×3=2619 → shifted by two →261,900. Correct.\n\nAdding: 6111+69840=75,951. 75,951+261,900=337,851. Yes.\n\nSo the final answer is 337,851. I think that\'s correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 873 and 387 is \\boxed{337851}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 873 and 387, we use the standard multiplication method, breaking it down step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 873 by the ones place digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   873 \\times 7 = 6111\n   \\]\n   - \\(3 \\times 7 = 21\\), write 1, carry over 2.\n   - \\(7 \\times 7 = 49 + 2 = 51\\), write 1, carry over 5.\n   - \\(8 \\times 7 = 56 + 5 = 61\\), write 1, carry over 6.\n   - Result: 6111.\n\n2. **Multiply 873 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   873 \\times 80 = 69840\n   \\]\n   - \\(3 \\times 8 = 24\\), write 4, carry over 2.\n   - \\(7 \\times 8 = 56 + 2 = 58\\), write 8, carry over 5.\n   - \\(8 \\times 8 = 64 + 5 = 69\\), write 9, carry over 6.\n   - Result: 6984. Shift one position left: 69840.\n\n3. **Multiply 873 by the hundreds place digit (300):**\n   \\[\n   873 \\times 300 = 261900\n   \\]\n   - \\(3 \\times 3 = 9\\).\n   - \\(7 \\times 3 = 21\\), write 1, carry over 2.\n   - \\(8 \\times 3 = 24 + 2 = 26\\), write 6, carry over 2.\n   - Result: 2619. Shift two positions left: 261900.\n\n4. **Sum all the partial results:**\n   \\[\n   6111 + 69840 + 261900 = 337851\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(6111 + 69840 = 75951\\).\n   - Then add \\(75951 + 261900 = 337851\\).\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{337851}\\).', ''] 39%|###8      | 193/500 [4:05:15<5:56:23, 69.65s/it]
