Correct.\n\nThen 61,656 + 513,800: 61,656 + 500,000 = 561,656, plus 13,800 is 575,456. So total is 575,456.\n\nWait a second, but let me confirm with another method, maybe the standard algorithm:\n\n   734\n\u00d7 784\n--------\n\nFirst, 734 \u00d7 4 = 2,936\n\nThen, 734 \u00d7 80 = 58,720 (shift one position to the left)\n\nThen, 734 \u00d7 700 = 513,800 (shift two positions left)\n\nAdding them:\n\n2,936\n58,720\n513,800\nTotal: 2,936 + 58,720 = 61,656; 61,656 + 513,800 = 575,456. Yes, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, using another method: (700 + 34) \u00d7 (700 + 84) but that might complicate. Alternatively, use the formula (a+b)(c+d) = ac + ad + bc + bd but perhaps overcomplicating.\n\nAlternatively, 734 \u00d7 784 = 734 \u00d7 (800 - 16) = 734\u00d7800 - 734\u00d716. Let's see:\n\n734 \u00d7 800 = 587,200\n\n734 \u00d716: 734\u00d710=7,340; 734\u00d76=4,404 \u2192 total 7,340+4,404=11,744\n\nSo 587,200 - 11,744 = 575,456. Same result. Good.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 575,456.\n\nBut wait, in my initial mistaken thought process I had some numbers that didn't make sense, but after correcting the problem to 734\u00d7784, the correct answer is 575,456. Let me ensure that in the template the numbers are correctly filled.\n\nThe user's question is:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 734 and 784?\n# Reasoning:\n\nSo following the template:\n\nLet me structure the reasoning as per the example given:\n\nOriginal example for 27 and 153:\n\n1. Multiply 27 by 3 (ones place of 153) \u2192 81\n2. Multiply 27 by 50 (tens place of 153) \u2192 1350\n3. Multiply 27 by 100 (hundreds place of 153) \u2192 2700\nSum: 81 + 1350 = 1431; 1431 + 2700 = 4131\n\nSo applying the same steps:\n\nFor 734 and 784:\n\n1. Multiply 734 by 4 (ones place of 784) \u2192 2936\n2. Multiply 734 by 80 (tens place of 784) \u2192 58,720\n3. Multiply 734 by 700 (hundreds place of 784) \u2192 513,800\nSum all three: 2936 + 58,720 = 61,656; 61,656 + 513,800 = 575,456\n\nSo the reasoning should be