at matches. I need to present it in that format.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 666 and 338?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 338 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.  \n1. Multiply 666 by the ones place digit 8 of 338:  \n   \\(666 \\times 8 = 5,\\!328\\).  \n2. Multiply 666 by the tens place digit 30 of 338:  \n   \\(666 \\times 30 = 19,\\!980\\).  \n3. Multiply 666 by the hundreds place digit 300 of 338:  \n   \\(666 \\times 300 = 199,\\!800\\).  \nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(5,\\!328 + 19,\\!980 + 199,\\!800 = 225,\\!108\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{225108}\\).", ''] 42%|####2     | 211/500 [4:24:47<6:17:40, 78.41s/it]
