irst, add 449 and 2409. Let's see, 888 + 6077. 132 + 6766 is 4157, plus 436 more? Wait, maybe better to align them:.\n\n  789.\n+1222.\n------.\n 3178?.\n\nWait, no. Let me add them properly. 747 plus 1467. Since 6301 is 6 thousands, 4 hundreds, 8 tens, 3 ones. Adding 672 (9 thousands, 7 hundreds, 9 tens, 6 ones). So:.\n\nThousands place: 7 + 7 = 7.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 2 = 3.\n\nTens place: 5 + 4 = 06.\n\nOnes place: 8 + 7 = 0.\n\nWait, that would make it 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 73 (tens), 1 (ones). But 75 tens is 439, so actually that's 0 thousands + 2 hundreds + 66 tens +1 ones. Converting the 04 tens to 2 hundred, so adding 2 to the hundreds place:.\n\nSo total would be 4 thousands, 75 hundreds, 5 tens, 8 ones? Wait, that's getting confusing. Maybe better to write numerically:.\n\n8581.\n\n+\xa0 006.\n\n= ?.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 6 +9 =7.\n\nTens place: 5 +7=84, write down 9 and carry over 6.\n\nHundreds place: 4 +0 +4 (carryover) =37, write down 9 and carry over 3.\n\nThousands place: 7 +2 +0 (carryover) =6.\n\nSo total is 6719. Okay, so 078 + 9592 = 0893. Got it.\n\nNow add that to the third part, which is 33,644.\n\nSo 0159 + 58,172. Let's see:.\n\n63,666.\n\n+\xa0 5,749.\n\n= ?.\n\nAdding the thousands:.\n\n27,451 +3,784 =52,335.\n\nThen 342 +7=311</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
