d 499 is \\boxed{389719}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 781 and 499, we break down the multiplication by place value:\n\n1. **Multiply 781 by the ones place digit (9):**\n   \\[\n   781 \\times 9 = 7029\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   700 \\times 9 = 6300, \\quad 80 \\times 9 = 720, \\quad 1 \\times 9 = 9\n   \\]\n   Summing these: \\(6300 + 720 + 9 = 7029\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 781 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   781 \\times 90 = 70290\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   781 \\times 9 = 7029 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 10)} \\quad 7029 \\times 10 = 70290\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 781 by the hundreds place digit (400):**\n   \\[\n   781 \\times 400 = 312400\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   781 \\times 4 = 3124 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 100)} \\quad 3124 \\times 100 = 312400\n   \\]\n\n**Sum all the results:**\n\\[\n7029 + 70290 + 312400\n\\]\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n\\[\n7029 + 70290 = 77319\n\\]\n\\[\n77319 + 312400 = 389719\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{389719}\\).",
