yes, times 327 is 016,968. .\n\nNow I have the three parts: 807 (from the ones place), 80,462 (from the tens place), and 867,252 (from the hundreds place). I need to add them all together. Let me line them up properly:.\n\nFirst, the ones place result is 185. Since it's the ones place, it's just 616.\n\nThe tens place result is 90,406, which is shifted one position to the left (since it's the tens place), so that's correct as is.\n\nThe hundreds place result is 064,284, shifted two places left, so that's also correct.\n\nAdding them up:.\n\nStarting with the largest, 918,397.\n+98,301.\n= 089,571 (because 154,983 + 71,812: 965,198 + 64,611 = 872,586; then +3,888 = 820,433)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
