the total is 386,264. Let me double-check the multiplication to ensure there are no errors.\n\nAlternatively, using another method: 424 \u00d7 911 can be computed as 424 \u00d7 (900 + 10 + 1) = 424\u00d7900 + 424\u00d710 + 424\u00d71, which is exactly what I did. The individual multiplications seem correct. 424 \u00d7 9 is indeed 3,816 (since 400\u00d79=3,600 and 24\u00d79=216; 3,600+216=3,816). Adding two zeros gives 381,600. Then 424\u00d710=4,240, and 424\u00d71=424. Adding all together gives 381,600 + 4,240 = 385,840; then +424 = 386,264. Yep, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 386,264.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 424 and 911 is \\boxed{386264}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 424 and 911, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of 911 (which is 900 + 10 + 1):\n\n1. Multiply 424 by the ones place digit (1):\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 1 = 424\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 424 by the tens place digit (10):\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 10 = 4240\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 424 by the hundreds place digit (900):\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 900 = 424 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 3816 \\times 100 = 381600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n424 + 4240 + 381600\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the ones and tens place multiplications:\n\\[\n424 + 4240 = 4664\n\\]\n\nThen add this result to the product of the hundreds place multiplication:\n\\[\n4664 + 381600 = 386264\n\\]\n\nThus, the final product of 424 and 911 is \\(\\boxed{386264}\\).",
