nLet me compute 744 \u00d7200 =148,800\n\n744 \u00d750=37,200\n\n744 \u00d79=6,696\n\nAdding them up: 148,800 +37,200 =186,000. Then +6,696 =192,696. Yes, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, 259 \u00d7700 = 181,300; 259\u00d740=10,360; 259\u00d74=1,036. Adding those: 181,300+10,360=191,660 +1,036=192,696. Same result.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 192,696.\n\nBut let me check again step-by-step as per the template:\n\nThe template example had:\n\nFor 27\u00d7153:\n\n1. 27\u00d73=81\n\n2. 27\u00d750=1350\n\n3. 27\u00d7100=2700\n\nSum: 81+1350=1431 +2700=4131.\n\nSo for the current problem 744\u00d7259:\n\nNumber2 is 259 (three digits), so three steps:\n\n1. Multiply 744 by 9 (ones place): 744\u00d79=6,696\n\n2. Multiply 744 by 50 (tens place): 744\u00d750=37,200\n\n3. Multiply 744 by 200 (hundreds place):744\u00d7200=148,800\n\nSum all three: 6,696 +37,200 =43,896 +148,800=192,696.\n\nYes, that's correct. So the final answer is 192,696.\n\nI think my initial confusion was due to the user's example having different numbers, but now focusing on the actual problem given, it's clear.\n</think>\n\n",
