n\nNow, sum all three parts:\n\n1378 (ones)\n+13,780 (tens)\n+620,100 (hundreds)\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 1378 + 13,780:\n\n1378 + 13,780 = 15,158.\n\nThen add 620,100:\n\n15,158 + 620,100 = 635,258.\n\nWait, let me check the addition again:\n\n13,780 + 1,378 = 15,158. Then 15,158 + 620,100:\n\n620,100 + 15,158:\n\n620,100 + 10,000 = 630,100\n\n630,100 + 5,158 = 635,258. Yes.\n\nSo the total is 635,258.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\nMultiply 689 \u00d7 922.\n\nFirst, write them down:\n\n      689\n    \u00d7922\n    -------\n\nMultiply 689 by 2 (units):\n\n689 \u00d72 = 1,378\n\nMultiply 689 by 20 (tens):\n\n689 \u00d720 = 13,780\n\nMultiply 689 by 900 (hundreds):\n\n689 \u00d7900 = 620,100\n\nAdding all together:\n\n1,378 +13,780 = 15,158\n\n15,158 + 620,100 = 635,258. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, using another approach: 689 \u00d7 922 = 689 \u00d7 (900 + 20 +2) = 689\u00d7900 + 689\u00d720 +689\u00d72, which is exactly what I did.\n\nSo the final product should be 635,258.\n\nWait, but let me check with calculator steps:\n\nLet me compute 689 \u00d7 922:\n\nFirst, compute 689 \u00d7 900 = 620,100\n\n689 \u00d7 22 = 689 \u00d720 +689\u00d72 =13,780 +1,378=15,158\n\nTotal 620,100 +15,158 =635,258. Yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 635,258.\n\nBut let me just ensure that I didn't make a mistake in any of the intermediate steps.\n\nWait, 689\u00d7900: 689\u00d79 is 6,201, so times 100 is 620,100. Correct.\n\n689\u00d720: 689\u00d72 is 1,378, so times 10 is 13,780. Correct.\n\n689\u00d72 is 1,378. Correct.\n\nAdding 1,378 +13,780: 1,378 +13,780 = 15,158. Then 15,158 +620,100: yes, 620,100 +15,000 is 635,100, plus 158 gives 635,258.\n\nAlright, that seems consistent. I think that's the correct answer. I don't see any errors in the calculations now.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 689 and 922 is \\boxed{635258}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 689 and 922?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 922 has three digits, so we can break down the multiplication into three steps based on place values.\n1. Multiply 689 by the ones place digit 2 of 922:\n   \\[\n   689 \\times 2 = 1378\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 689 by the tens place digit 20 of 922:\n   \\[\n   689 \\times 20 = 13780\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 689 by the hundreds place digit 900 of 922:\n   \\[\n   689 \\times 900 = 620100\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n1378 + 13780 + 620100 = 635258\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is 635258.\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 689 and 922 is \\boxed{635258}.",
