rrect. But in the initial problem statement, the user had a template with 27 and 153, and then the actual question is 361 and 743. The user wants the reasoning filled in as per the template. So following the template steps:\n\n1. Multiply 361 by the ones digit 3 of 743: 361\u00d73=1,083.\n\n2. Multiply 361 by the tens digit 4 (but since it's the tens place, it's actually 40): 361\u00d740=14,440.\n\n3. Multiply 361 by the hundreds digit 7 (which is 700): 361\u00d7700=252,700.\n\nSum all the step results: 1,083 +14,440 +252,700 = 268,223.\n\nSo the final answer is 268,223. I need to present this in the template format as the user specified.\n</think>\n\n",
