g the standard algorithm:\n\nFirst, write 203\n\n× 373\n\n________\n\nMultiply 203 by 3: 609\n\nMultiply 203 by 70: 14,210 (shifted one position to the left)\n\nMultiply 203 by 300: 60,900 (shifted two positions to the left)\n\nAdding those together:\n\n   609\n\n+14,210\n\n=14,819\n\n14,819 + 60,900 = 75,719. Yes, that matches.\n\nWait a second, but let me do it another way to cross-verify. Maybe using distributive property:\n\n203 × 373 = 203 × (300 + 70 + 3) = 203×300 + 203×70 + 203×3 = same as above, which gives 60,900 + 14,210 + 609 = 75,719.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another multiplication method. Let me try breaking down 373 as 400 - 27. Wait, 373 is 400 - 27. Hmm, but not sure if that helps, but let's see:\n\n203 × (400 - 27) = 203×400 - 203×27.\n\n203×400 = 81,200\n\n203×27: 200×27=5,400 and 3×27=81, so total 5,481.\n\nSo 81,200 - 5,481 = 75,719. Yep, same result. Okay, that's a good check.\n\nTherefore, the final product should be 75,719.\n\nBut wait, in my initial wrong thinking process, I had different numbers. But after correcting, I think it's right. So the answer is 75,719.\n\nWait another thought: Let me compute 203 × 373 step by step again carefully.\n\nAlternatively, compute 373 × 200 = 74,600 and 373 × 3 = 1,119. Adding those together: 74,600 + 1,119 = 75,719. Exactly the same. Okay, so confident now.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 75,719. I need to present this in the template given, following the structure of the example provided.\n\nThe example had:\n\nReasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n\n1. Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153\n\n2. Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153\n\n(other digits if needed)\n\nThen sum the results.\n\nSo following that structure for the question with 203 and 373:\n\nThe number2 here is 373, which has three digits. So three steps: ones (3), tens (70), hundreds (300). So:\n\nStep 1: Multiply