      "text": "20736. Wait, but I think I'm getting confused here. Let me try with the given problem in the template.\n\nWait, the user provided an example where the question was 27 \u00d7 153, and the reasoning was:\n\n1. 27\u00d73=81,\n\n2. 27\u00d750=1350,\n\n3. 27\u00d7100=2700,\n\nsum them: 81+1350=1431, +2700=4131.\n\nSo the key is breaking down the second number into hundreds, tens, ones, then multiplying each part by the first number and summing.\n\nSo applying that to the current problem: 119 \u00d7 239.\n\nFirst, break down 239 into 200 + 30 +9.\n\nThen:\n\n1. 119 \u00d79 = ?\n\n119\u00d79: 100\u00d79=900, 19\u00d79=171 \u2192 total 1071.\n\n2. 119\u00d730 = 119\u00d73\u00d710 = 357\u00d710=3570.\n\n3. 119\u00d7200 = 119\u00d72\u00d7100=238\u00d7100=23800.\n\nNow sum all three:\n\n1071 + 3570 = 4641,\n\n4641 +23800 = 28441.\n\nWait, but let me check that again:\n\nFirst step: 119\u00d79:\n\n119\u00d79: 100\u00d79=900; 19\u00d79=171 \u2192 900+171=1071. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 119\u00d730: 119\u00d73=357 \u2192 \u00d710 is 3570. Correct.\n\nThird step: 119\u00d7200: 119\u00d72=238 \u2192 \u00d7100 is 23800. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 1071 +3570 = 4641; 4641 +23800 = 28441.\n\nWait, but 119 \u00d7239. Let me verify with another method. Let's compute 119 \u00d7240 = 119\u00d724\u00d710. 24\u00d7100=2400, 24\u00d719=456 \u2192 total 2400+456=2856 \u2192 \u00d710? Wait no, 24\u00d7119: 24\u00d7100=2400, 24\u00d719=456 \u2192 total 2856. So 119\u00d7240 is 119\u00d724\u00d710? Wait, no, 240 is 24\u00d710, so 119\u00d7240 = (119\u00d724)*10 \u2192 2856\u00d710=28560. But since we want 119\u00d7239 = 119\u00d7(240-1) = 28560 -119 = 28560-100=28460, minus 19 more \u2192 28460-19=28441. So that matches the previous result. So the answer is 28441.\n\nTherefore, following the template:\n\nThe problem is \"What is the product of 119 and 239?\"\n\nReasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. 239 has three digits, so three steps:\n\n1. Multiply 119 by the ones digit 9: 119\u00