First, 449 \u00d7800 = 449 \u00d78 \u00d7100 = 3,592 \u00d7100 = 359,200.\n\n449 \u00d720 = 8,980.\n\n449 \u00d73 = 1,347.\n\nAdding those: 359,200 +8,980 = 368,180. Then 368,180 +1,347 = 369,527. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the correct product is 369,527. The initial thought process had some errors in the steps but arrived at the correct answer eventually. The key steps are breaking down the multiplication into the three digits of 823 (3, 20, 800), multiplying each by 449, then adding the results.\n</think>\n\n",
