git (3):  \n   \\(128 \\times 3 = 384\\).\n2. Multiply 128 by the tens place digit (20):  \n   \\(128 \\times 20 = 2,\\!560\\).\n3. Multiply 128 by the hundreds place digit (900):  \n   \\(128 \\times 900 = 115,\\!200\\).\n\nSum all the step results:  \n\\(384 + 2,\\!560 + 115,\\!200 = 118,\\!144\\).\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(384 + 2,\\!560 + 115,\\!200 = 118,\\!144\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{118144}.", '']
