ing the intermediate products. So the correct answer is 122,298.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 218 and 561 is \\boxed{122298}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 218 and 561, we can break down the multiplication step by step using the standard algorithm.\n\n1. **Multiply 218 by the ones place digit (1) of 561:**\n   \\[\n   218 \\times 1 = 218\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 218 by the tens place digit (60) of 561:**\n   \\[\n   218 \\times 60 = 13,080\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 218 by the hundreds place digit (500) of 561:**\n   \\[\n   218 \\times 500 = 109,000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results from the steps above:\n\\[\n218 + 13,080 + 109,000\n\\]\n\nAdding these step by step:\n\\[\n218 + 13,080 = 13,298\n\\]\n\\[\n13,298 + 109,000 = 122,298\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 218 and 561 is \\(\\boxed{122298}\\).",
