swer**\nThe product of 531 and 265 is \\boxed{140715}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 531 and 265, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 531 by the ones place digit (5):**\n   \\[\n   531 \\times 5 = 2655\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 531 by the tens place digit (60):**\n   \\[\n   531 \\times 6 = 3186 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero for the tens place)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 31860\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 531 by the hundreds place digit (200):**\n   \\[\n   531 \\times 2 = 1062 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros for the hundreds place)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 106200\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results from the steps above:\n\\[\n2655 + 31860 + 106200\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the ones and tens place multiplications:\n\\[\n2655 + 31860 = 34515\n\\]\n\nThen add the result of the hundreds place multiplication:\n\\[\n34515 + 106200 = 140715\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 531 and 265 is \\(\\boxed{140715}\\).", '']
