p reasoning is correct.\n\nBut let me check the initial steps again as per the template. The user\'s example had steps for multiplying by each digit with their place values. So in the example, number2 was 153 (so 3 ones, 5 tens, 1 hundred). Then step1: multiply by 3 (ones), step2 multiply by 50 (tens), step3 multiply by 100 (hundreds). So for 599, it\'s 9 ones, 9 tens, 5 hundreds, so steps would be:\n\nStep1: 196×9 = 1,764\n\nStep2: 196×90 = 17,640\n\nStep3: 196×500 = 98,000\n\nAdding those gives 1,764 +17,640 = 19,404 +98,000 = 117,404. Correct.\n\nSo the answer is 117,404. Therefore, I need to present this in the template.\n\nWait, but in the user\'s example, the answer section had "sum of the results" and then the final answer. So the answer part should look like:\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: 1,764 + 17,640 + 98,000 = 117,404.\nSo, the final computed product is 117,404.\n\nAlright, that seems correct. Let me make sure I didn\'t make any calculation errors in the steps.\n\nCalculating step1 again: 196×9.\n\n196×9:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n100×9 = 900,\n\n90×9 = 810,\n\n6×9 = 54.\n\nAdding them: 900+810 is 1,710, plus 54 is 1,764. Correct.\n\nStep2: 196×90.\n\nSince 90 is 9×10, so 1,764 ×10 =17,640. Correct.\n\nStep3: 196×500.\n\n196×5=980, so ×100=98,000. Correct.\n\nSumming them:\n\n1,764 +17,640: 1,764+17,640. Let\'s add 1,764 +17,640:\n\n1,764 + 17,640:\n\nAdding thousands: 1,000 +17,000 =18,000.\n\nHundreds: 700 + 600 = 1,300 → total 19,300?\n\nWait, wait:\n\nWait 1,764 is 1 thousand 7 hundreds 64.\n\n17,640 is 17 thousands 6 hundreds 40.\n\nAdding them:\n\nThousands: 1+17 =18\n\nHundreds:7+6=13 → so 18,000 + 1,300 =19,300\n\nTens and units:64+40=104 → 19,300 +104=19,404.\n\nThen adding 98,000:\n\n19,404 +98,000 = 117,404. All correct.\n\nYes, so the answer is correct.\n\nI think that\'s all. The key steps are breaking down each digit with its place value, multiplying each, then adding. Also, the alternative method using distributive property (599=600-1)