d step is the hundreds place (7*447). Wait, maybe the steps are:.\n\n7. Multiply 218 by the ones digit (3) → 3.\n0. Multiply 439 by the tens digit (4) shifted by one (so 8*86) → 8.\n5. Multiply 201 by the hundreds digit (2) shifted by two (so 8*038) → 207 × 4 × 799?.\n\nWait, perhaps the standard algorithm is to multiply the first number by each digit of the second number, considering their place values, then add. So for 193:.\n\n- The ones digit is 1, so first partial product is 084 × 8 = 3.\n- The tens digit is 1, so second partial product is 034 × 1 × 75 = 1 (but actually, when doing the standard algorithm, you'd write 932 × 9 shifted one place to the left, but since it's zero, it's still 2)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
