e initial steps had some errors in the thought process but ended up with the right answer. The key is to break down each digit's contribution properly and sum them. So the correct product is 423,273.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 709 and 597 is \\boxed{423273}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 709 and 597, we break down the multiplication into three parts based on the digits of 597 (500, 90, and 7):\n\n1. Multiply 709 by 7:\n   \\[\n   709 \\times 7 = 4,963\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 709 by 90 (which is 9 \u00d7 10):\n   \\[\n   709 \\times 9 = 6,381 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 10)} \\quad 6,381 \\times 10 = 63,810\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 709 by 500 (which is 5 \u00d7 100):\n   \\[\n   709 \\times 5 = 3,545 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 100)} \\quad 3,545 \\times 100 = 354,500\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three multiplications:\n\\[\n4,963 + 63,810 + 354,500\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the first two results:\n\\[\n4,963 + 63,810 = 68,773\n\\]\n\nThen add the third result:\n\\[\n68,773 + 354,500 = 423,273\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 709 and 597 is \\(\\boxed{423273}\\).",
