housands place)=14 +1 (carry)=15 \u2192 write 5, carryover1.\n\n5 (ten thousands place) +7 (ten thousands place) =12 +1=13 \u2192 write 3 and carryover1. Since there are no more digits, the carryover1 becomes the next digit.\n\nSo total is 135,708.\n\nWait, so 56,808 +78,900 is 135,708.\n\nTherefore, the total product of 789 \u00d7172 is 135,708.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, compute 789 \u00d7172:\n\nFirst, 789\u00d7100=78,900\n\n789\u00d770=55,230\n\n789\u00d72=1,578\n\nAdding them: 78,900 +55,230 = 134,130. Then +1,578 \u2192 134,130 +1,578 = 135,708. Yes, that matches.\n\nAlternatively, using another method: (700 +80 +9)(100 +70 +2). But that might be more complicated.\n\nAlternatively, verify with calculator steps:\n\n789 \u00d7 172.\n\nLet me compute 789 \u00d7 172:\n\nFirst, 789 \u00d7 100 = 78,900\n\n789 \u00d7 70 = 55,230 (since 789\u00d77=5,523, \u00d710 is 55,230)\n\n789 \u00d72 =1,578\n\nAdding all: 78,900 +55,230 = 134,130; 134,130 +1,578 = 135,708. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 135,708. So in the template, the steps would be as follows:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 789 and 172?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 172 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 789 by the ones place digit 2 of 172: 789 \u00d7 2 = 1,578.\n2. Multiply 789 by the tens place digit 70 of 172: 789 \u00d7 70 = 55,230.\n3. Multiply 789 by the hundreds place digit 100 of 172: 789 \u00d7 100 = 78,900.\nNow, sum all the step results: 1,578 + 55,230 + 78,900 = 135,708.\nSo, the final computed product is 135708.\n\nWait, but in the template answer, the user's example had the sum written out with the numbers, so maybe we should write it as 1,578 + 55,230 = 56,808; then 56,808 + 78,900 = 135,708. But the main thing is the final answer.\n\nBut the user's example had \"sum of the results\" as a line, so probably the steps are correct as listed.\n\nI need to make sure that in the reason