57 and 952 is \\boxed{625464}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 657 and 952?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step.\n1. Multiply 657 by the ones place digit 2 of 952: \\(657 \\times 2 = 1314\\)\n2. Multiply 657 by the tens place digit 50 of 952: \\(657 \\times 50 = 32850\\)\n3. Multiply 657 by the hundreds place digit 900 of 952: \\(657 \\times 900 = 591300\\)\nSum all the results: \\(1314 + 32850 = 34164\\); \\(34164 + 591300 = 625464\\)\nAnswer: The final computed product is 625464.\n# \n\nThe product of 657 and 952 is \\boxed{625464}.", ''] 72%|#######1  | 358/500 [7:07:02<2:53:11, 73.18s/it]
