t's count:.\n\nDigits of 422,888:  .\nHundred thousands: 0  .\nTen thousands:4  .\nThousands:2  .\nHundreds:3  .\nTens:8  .\nOnes:9  .\n\nDigits of 99,407:  .\nTen thousands:9  .\nThousands:5  .\nHundreds:3  .\nTens:5  .\nOnes:4  .\n\nWait, actually, perhaps aligning:.\n\n959928  .\n+\xa0 40187  .\n=  .\nSo:.\n\n840081  .\n+\xa0 94940  .\n_________  .\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 2 +9=3  .\nTens:2 +5=8  .\nHundreds:8 +6=34 → 9, carryover 8  .\nThousands:2 +7=8 plus 8 →4  .\nTen thousands:2 (from 370331's ten thousands place?) Wait, 147,931 has ten thousands digit as 7? Wait, 690,471 is 7 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 8 (ones). So when adding to 01,749 which is 6 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 3 (ones). .\n\nSo the ten thousands place for 450681 is 3 (since it's 793,261 +9,711), so the ten thousands digit is 6. The ten thousands digit in 14,453 is 4. So adding ten thousands: 7 +8=8. .\n\nHundred thousands place: 6 (from 411,493) + 1 (from 66,143) =1. .\n\nPutting it all together: .\n\nHundred thousands: 7  .\nTen thousands:1  .\nThousands:2  .\nHundreds:9 (from the carryover)  .\nTens:3  .\nOnes:8  .\n\nWait, let me recheck:.\n\nAfter thousands place: 4 (from 857863's thousands digit) plus 7 (from 77,323's thousands digit) is 1 plus the carryover 8 makes 4. .\n\nThen ten thousands place: 8 (from 438515's ten thousands digit) + 5 (from 84,613's ten thousands digit) = 8.\n\nHundred thousands: 4 (from 548543) plus nothing, so 6</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
