ep.\n1. Multiply 27 by 3 (ones place) → 81\n2. Multiply 27 by 50 (tens place) → 1350\n3. Multiply 27 by 100 (hundreds place) → 2700\nSum all results: 81 + 1350 +2700 = 4131\n\nAnswer: 4131\n\nSo following that structure for 939 ×387:\n\nBreaking 387 into 300+80+7, so:\n\n1. Multiply 939 by 7 (ones place) → 6,573\n\n2. Multiply 939 by 80 (tens place) → 75,120\n\n3. Multiply 939 by 300 (hundreds place) → 281,700\n\nSum: 6,573 +75,120 =81,693; then 81,693 +281,700 =363,393.\n\nSo the reasoning steps should be written accordingly. I need to make sure each step is clearly broken down as per the template.\n\nI think that's all. The answer is 363,393.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 939 and 387 is \\boxed{363393}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 939 and 387?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 387 has three digits, so we can break it down into 300, 80, and 7, and multiply each part by 939.\n1. Multiply 939 by the ones place digit 7 of 387:\n   \\[\n   939 \\times 7 = 6573\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 939 by the tens place digit 80 of 387:\n   \\[\n   939 \\times 80 = 75120\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 939 by the hundreds place digit 300 of 387:\n   \\[\n   939 \\times 300 = 281700\n   \\]\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n6573 + 75120 + 281700 = 363393\n\\]\nSo, the final computed product is 363393.\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 939 and 387 is \\boxed{363393}.", ''] 73%|#######2  | 363/500 [7:12:22<2:31:15, 66.24s/it]
