before). \n\n402\u00d74=1,608. \n\nAdding those three: 120,600 +32,160=152,760. Then 152,760 +1,608 =154,368. So yes, same.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 154,368.\n\nWait, in my first calculation, when I broke down (400+2)(300+80+4), the total was 154,368, so that matches. So I think that's correct.\n\nI think that's thorough. So following the template, the steps are:\n\n1. Multiply 402 by 4 (ones place) = 1,608\n\n2. Multiply 402 by 80 (tens place) = 32,160\n\n3. Multiply 402 by 300 (hundreds place) = 120,600\n\nSum them: 1,608 +32,160 =33,768; 33,768 +120,600=154,368\n\nTherefore, the product is 154,368.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 402 and 384 is \\boxed{154368}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 402 and 384, we break it down into three steps based on the digits of 384 (3 hundreds, 8 tens, and 4 ones):\n\n1. **Multiply 402 by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 4 = 1608\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 402 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 80 = 32160\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 402 by the hundreds place digit (300):**\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 300 = 120600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n1608 + 32160 + 120600\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the first two results:\n\\[\n1608 + 32160 = 33768\n\\]\n\nThen add the third result:\n\\[\n33768 + 120600 = 154368\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 402 and 384 is \\(\\boxed{154368}\\).",
