over 8.\n\n9 × 6 = 54, plus 8 is 62. Write down 2, carryover 6. No more digits, so write the 6.\n\nSo 692 × 9 = 6,228. Then multiply by 100 (shift two places): 622,800.\n\nNow, add up all three results:\n\nFirst: 4,152\n\nSecond: 13,840\n\nThird: 622,800\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\nFirst, add 4,152 + 13,840.\n\n4,152 + 13,840 = 17,992.\n\nThen add that to 622,800:\n\n17,992 + 622,800 = 640,792.\n\nWait, is that correct? Let me verify using another method.\n\nAlternatively, compute 692 × 926:\n\nWe can use the standard multiplication:\n\n     692\n\n   × 926\n\n   ---------\n\nFirst, multiply by 6: 692×6=4,152\n\nThen multiply by 20: 692×20=13,840\n\nThen multiply by 900: 692×900=622,800\n\nAdding them together: 4,152 + 13,840 = 17,992; 17,992 + 622,800 = 640,792.\n\nHmm, but let me check with another approach, perhaps the distributive property:\n\n692 × 926 = 692 × (900 + 26) = 692×900 + 692×26.\n\nWait, but that might complicate. Alternatively, compute 692×926 directly:\n\nAlternatively, use calculator-like approach:\n\n692 × 926.\n\nLet me compute 692 × 926:\n\nFirst, note that 692 × 900 = 622,800\n\n692 × 26 = ?\n\n692 × 20 = 13,840\n\n692 × 6 = 4,152\n\nSo 13,840 + 4,152 = 18, 992\n\nWait, 13,840 + 4,152 = 17,992? Wait, 13,840 + 4,152:\n\n13,840 + 4,000 = 17,840\n\nThen +152 = 17,992. So total is 622,800 + 17,992 = 640,792. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made a mistake in the first calculation. Let me confirm with another method.\n\nAlternatively, use the formula (a+b)(c+d) but not sure.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps check with approximate values.\n\n692 is close to 700, and 926 is close to 900. 700×900 = 630,000. Since 692 is 8 less than 700, and 926 is 26 more than 900, so the exact difference would be:\n\n(700 -8)(900 +26) = 700×900 +700×26 -8×900 -8×26\n\n= 630,000 + 18,200 -7,200 -208\n\nCompute step by step:\n\n630,000 +18,200 = 648,200\n\n648,200 -7,200 = 641,000\n\n641,000 - 208 = 640,792. Which matches. So the answer is 640,792.\n\nTherefore, 