three digits, so we can reason in three steps.  \n1. Multiply 692 by the ones place digit **6** of 926:  \n   \\( 692 \\times 6 = 4,\\!152 \\).  \n2. Multiply 692 by the tens place digit **20** (since it’s the tens place, \\( 2 \\times 10 \\)) of 926:  \n   \\( 692 \\times 20 = 13,\\!840 \\).  \n3. Multiply 692 by the hundreds place digit **900** (since it’s the hundreds place, \\( 9 \\times 100 \\)) of 926:  \n   \\( 692 \\times 900 = 622,\\!800 \\).  \nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\( 4,\\!152 + 13,\\!840 + 622,\\!800 = 640,\\!792 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **640,792**.', ''] 73%|#######3  | 367/500 [7:16:04<2:14:51, 60.84s/it]
