916 by the ones place digit (1) of 971:**\n   \\[\n   916 \\times 1 = 916\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 916 by the tens place digit (70) of 971:**\n   \\[\n   916 \\times 70 = 916 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 6412 \\times 10 = 64120\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 916 by the hundreds place digit (900) of 971:**\n   \\[\n   916 \\times 900 = 916 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 8244 \\times 100 = 824400\n   \\]\n\n**Summing all the partial products:**\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n916 \\quad \\text{(ones place)} \\\\\n+ 64120 \\quad \\text{(tens place)} \\\\\n+ 824400 \\quad \\text{(hundreds place)} \\\\\n\\hline\n889436\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 916 and 971 is \\(\\boxed{889436}\\).",
