it's 863,876. So the final answer should be 863,876.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 898 and 962 is \\boxed{863876}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 898 and 962, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 898 by the ones place digit (2) of 962:**\n   \\[\n   898 \\times 2 = 1796\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 898 by the tens place digit (60) of 962:**\n   \\[\n   898 \\times 60 = 898 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 5388 \\times 10 = 53880\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 898 by the hundreds place digit (900) of 962:**\n   \\[\n   898 \\times 900 = 898 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 8082 \\times 100 = 808200\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results from the steps above:\n\\[\n1796 + 53880 + 808200\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the first two results:\n\\[\n1796 + 53880 = 55676\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to the third result:\n\\[\n55676 + 808200 = 863876\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{863876}\\).",
