s: 0 + 16,750 + 234,500. Adding 16,750 + 234,500 gives 251,250. So the total is 251,250.\n\nWait, that seems correct. Let me verify with another method. 335 × 750 can also be written as 335 × (700 + 50 + 0) = 335×700 + 335×50 + 335×0. Which is exactly what I did.\n\nAlternatively, 335 × 750 = 335 × 75 ×10. Let's compute 335 ×75 first. 335×70=23,450 and 335×5=1,675. Adding those gives 23,450 +1,675=25,125. Then multiply by 10: 251,250. Yep, same result. So the answer should be 251,250.\n\nBut let me check once more step by step as per the template:\n\nNumber1 is 335, number2 is 750. Since number2 has three digits, three steps:\n\n1. Multiply 335 by the ones place digit (0): 335×0=0\n\n2. Multiply 335 by the tens place digit (50): 335×50=16,750\n\n3. Multiply 335 by the hundreds place digit (700): 335×700=234,500\n\nAdding all three: 0 +16,750 +234,500=251,250. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the final answer is 251,250. I think that's accurate now.\n</think>", '']
