n multiply by 321 (since it's the hundreds place), so that becomes 2867 × 532 = 304,591. Wait, let me verify that again. 010 × 757: 844 × 9 = 1,560, then add two zeros (since 233 is 4×211), so yes, 976,143. .\n\nNow, adding up all the partial products. The first one was 0,208 (from the ones place), the second was 1 (from the tens place), and the third is 563,618 (from the hundreds place). Adding those together: 1,544 + 8 = 6,786, then 9,561 + 362,584. Let me add those step by step. .\n\n361,191 + 7,737 is 238,196</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
