0 = 38,052. Then 38,052 + 483,200. 483,200 + 38,000 = 521,200, then plus 52 gives 521,252. Yes.\n\nTherefore, the final product should be 521,252.\n\nBut wait, let me verify this with another method to ensure I didn\'t make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, using standard multiplication:\n\n604 × 863.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n       604\n    × 863\n    --------\nFirst, multiply by 3 (ones place):\n\n604 × 3 = 1,812\n\nThen multiply by 60 (tens place, so shifted one position):\n\n604 × 6 = 3,624 → but since it\'s 60, it\'s 3,624 ×10 = 36,240\n\nThen multiply by 800 (hundreds place, shifted two positions):\n\n604 × 8 = 4,832 → times 100 is 483,200\n\nAdding all three:\n\n1,812 + 36,240 = 38,052\n\n38,052 + 483,200 = 521,252. That seems correct.\n\nWait a second, but I think I might have miscalculated 604 × 800. Let me check that again. 600×800 = 480,000, and 4×800=3,200. So total 480,000 + 3,200 = 483,200. That\'s correct.\n\nSo the answer should be 521,252.\n\nBut let me confirm with another approach. Let\'s compute 604 × 863 using the distributive property:\n\n604 × (800 + 60 + 3) = 604×800 + 604×60 + 604×3 = 483,200 + 36,240 + 1,812 = yes, same as before.\n\nAdding them:\n\n483,200 + 36,240 = 519,440\n\n519,440 + 1,812 = 521,252.\n\nYes, that\'s consistent. So the final answer is 521,252. I think that\'s correct. I don\'t see any errors in the steps now.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 604 and 863 is \\boxed{521252}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 604 and 863, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of 863:\n\n1. Multiply 604 by the ones place digit (3) of 863:\n   \\[\n   604 \\times 3 = 1812\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 604 by the tens place digit (60) of 863:\n   \\[\n   604 \\times 60 = 604 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 3624 \\times 10 = 36240\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 604 by the hundreds place digit (800) of 863:\n   \\[\n   604 \\times 800 = 604 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 4832 \\times 100 = 483200\n   \\]\n\nSum all the results from the steps:\n\\[\n1812 +