 10? So 701 * 0 *10 = 0.\n\n3. Multiply 701 by the hundreds place digit (9) times 100. So 701 * 9 * 100.\n\nThen adding all three results: 0 + 0 + (701*9*100). Let's compute that.\n\nFirst, 701 * 9: as before, 700*9=6300, 1*9=9, so 6309. Then times 100 is 630900. Adding the other zeros gives the same result. So that works.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 630,900. The initial methods all agree. I think that's correct. Let me just confirm once more with another method, maybe using the standard algorithm:\n\n   701\nx 900\n-------\n   000  (701 x 0)\n  000   (701 x 0, shifted one position to the left)\n6309    (701 x 9, shifted two positions to the left)\n-------\n630900\n\nYes, that's right. All the steps add up. So the final answer should be 630,900.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 701 and 900 is \\boxed{630900}.\n\n\n",
