28  \n—————  \n\u2003896 \xa0\xa0(112×8)  \n\u20032240 \xa0\xa0(112×20, shifted one left)  \n78400 \xa0\xa0(112×700, shifted two left)  \n—————  \nTotal: 896 + 2240 = 3136; 3136 +78400 = 81536. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 81,536.\n\nBut let me check once more with another approach. Let's compute 112 × 700 = 78,400. Then 112 ×28 = ?\n\n112 ×28: 100×28=2,800; 12×28=336. So 2,800 + 336 = 3,136. Then total is 78,400 + 3,136 = 81,536. Yep, same result.\n\nOkay, confident that the answer is correct.\n</think>", '']
