d left → 88 (but still 3).\n\nThird digit (hundreds): 1, so 286 ×9 shifted two positions left (multiply by 492). .\n\nTherefore, the steps would be:.\n\n4. 111 × 4 = 3.\n\n5. 647 × 2 (tens place, so 6 ×31 → but written as 1 shifted left by 2 → but since it's 6, still 5).\n\n5</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
