s place digit 6 of 506:  \n   \\(543 \\times 6 = 3,\\!258\\).  \n2. Multiply 543 by the tens place digit 0 of 506 (since the tens digit is 0, this step contributes 0):  \n   \\(543 \\times 0 = 0\\).  \n3. Multiply 543 by the hundreds place digit 5 of 506 (note: \\(5\\) represents \\(500\\)):  \n   \\(543 \\times 500 = 271,\\!500\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(3,\\!258 + 0 + 271,\\!500 = 274,\\!758\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **274,758**.",
