 results together:\n\n3,678 (from ones)\n\n+55,170 (from tens)\n\n+490,400 (from hundreds)\n\nLet me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 3,678 + 55,170:\n\n3,678 + 55,170 = 58,848.\n\nThen add 490,400 to that:\n\n58,848 + 490,400 = 549,248.\n\nWait, but let me check the addition again:\n\n3,678 +55,170:\n\n3,000 +55,000 =58,000,\n\n678 +170=848,\n\nTotal 58,848. Then 58,848 +490,400:\n\n58,848 + 490,400 = 549,248.\n\nHmm, but let me verify using another method to ensure accuracy.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n     613\n\n   ×896\n\n   --------\n\nFirst, multiply 613 by 6:\n\n6×3=18 (write 8, carryover 1)\n\n6×1=6 +1=7\n\n6×6=36. So first partial product is 3678.\n\nSecond, multiply 613 by 90 (the 9 in the tens place, so shifted one position):\n\n9×3=27 (write 7, carryover 2)\n\n9×1=9 +2=11 (write 1, carryover 1)\n\n9×6=54 +1=55. So this gives 5517, but shifted one place to the left, so 55,170.\n\nThird, multiply 613 by 800 (the 8 in the hundreds place, shifted two positions):\n\n8×3=24 (write 4, carryover 2)\n\n8×1=8 +2=10 (write 0, carryover 1)\n\n8×6=48 +1=49. So this gives 4904, shifted two places becomes 490,400.\n\nAdding them all together as before gives 3678 +55,170 =58,848; then +490,400 =549,248.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 549,248.\n\nWait, but let me do a quick check using another method, like the distributive property:\n\n613 ×896 = 613 ×(900 -4) = 613×900 -613×4.\n\nCompute 613×900 = 551,700.\n\n613×4 = 2,452.\n\nSubtract: 551,700 -2,452 = 549,248. Yes, same result. So that\'s correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 549,248.\n\nBut let me also check the initial steps in case of miscalculation.\n\nWait in the first step, 613×6: 600×6=3600, 13×6=78, total 3678. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 613×90: 613×9=5517, ×10=55,170. Correct.\n\nThird step: 613×800: 613×8=4904, ×100=490,400. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 3678 +55,170 =58,848. Then 58,848 +490,400: 58,848 +490,400 =549,248. Correct.\n\nOkay, so that seems accurate. Therefore, the final answer is 549,248.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 613 and 896 is \\boxed{549248}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 613 and 896, we can break down 896 into its place values (800, 90, and 6) and multiply each part by 613, then sum the results.\n\n1. Multiply 613 by the ones place digit (6):\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 6 = 3678\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 613 by the tens place digit (90):\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 90 = 613 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 5517 \\times 10 = 55170\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 613 by the hundreds place digit (800):\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 800 = 613 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 4904 \\times 100 = 490400\n   \\]\n\nAdding all the partial products together:\n\\[\n3678 + 55170 + 490400 = 549248\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 613 and 896 is \\(\\boxed{549248}\\).', '']100%|#########9| 499/500 [9:45:01<01:52, 112.91s/it]
